// The world this guest is compiled against, and the one place js-asset differs
// from the other three guests before a line of code is written.
//
// `asset-plugin` is the contract. This world adds nothing to it that a host can
// see: the exports are `asset-plugin`'s exports, unchanged, and
// `crates/host/tests/asset_e2e.rs` calls them by the same names it calls the
// Rust and C++ guests by.
//
// # Why it exists at all
//
// `lut` opens a file. Rust's `std::fs` and wasi-libc's `fopen` reach the
// filesystem through imports their runtimes declare, so `rust-asset` and
// `cpp-asset` never say the word `wasi:filesystem` anywhere -- it is simply in
// the binary their toolchain produced.
//
// A ComponentizeJS guest has no such runtime. StarlingMonkey exposes no file
// API to JavaScript at all -- `fetch`, `crypto`, `TextDecoder`, no `fs` -- and
// the only WASI a guest module may `import` is what the *world* declares.
// (Importing `wasi:filesystem/preopens@0.2.10` against the bare `asset-plugin`
// world fails at Wizer time with "Error loading module ... No such file or
// directory": the splicer registers a synthetic module per world import, and
// there was no such import to register.)
//
// So the filesystem has to be asked for out loud. That is the honest shape of
// this guest's bill, and `examples/policies/js-asset.toml` grants exactly it.
//
// # Why the version is 0.2.10
//
// StarlingMonkey already imports `wasi:filesystem/types@0.2.10` for its own
// module resolution. Naming the same interface at the same version means
// wit-component merges the two into one import rather than leaving the
// component asking for two versions of one thing. See `wit/deps/filesystem.wit`
// for where the text came from.
package watoots:js-asset@0.1.0;

world js-asset-plugin {
  // The contract, unmodified. `examples/wit/asset` is reached through a
  // symlink at `wit/deps/asset`, not a copy: a second copy of the world is a
  // second thing to keep in step, and this guest exists to prove it is the
  // same world.
  include watoots:asset/asset-plugin@0.1.0;

  // What `lut` needs, and the reason this file is not just an `include`.
  import wasi:filesystem/types@0.2.10;
  import wasi:filesystem/preopens@0.2.10;
}
